  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Voluntary Contributions to UN Agencies</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">An effective UN development system supports, at the global, regional and national levels, the achievement of the SDGs in developing countries. &#x2022; Normative support is provided by the UN development system to continue to develop and monitor the implementation of global standards in various areas such as human rights, environment, health, refugees etc. &#x2022; Preparedness of the UN system to respond to conflict, disaster or other humanitarian catastrophes in the poorest countries is improved.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support is provided to a set of UN agencies whose work aligns closely to the priorities of Ireland&#x2019;s international development policy, A Better World - gender equality, climate action, strengthened governance, climate action and reducing humanitarian need. Contributions to these UN agencies are generally un-earmarked (directed to their core budgets), allowing them to plan and manage resources effectively in support of the policy objectives set out in their strategic plans. Grantees include UNDP, OHCHR, UNFPA, UN Women, UN Volunteers and UNICEF.</narrative>
  </description>
